"""
Deepfake image detection with the official Vision Transformer (ViT-B/16)
Dataset : prithivMLmods/OpenDeepfake-Preview (Hugging Face)
Model   : Google Research vision_transformer (JAX/Flax), ImageNet-21k weights

This single file collects every code cell of the project notebook in running
order. It is written for Google Colab (T4 GPU). Cells are separated by
"# %%" markers, so VS Code / Jupytext / Colab can also treat it as a notebook.

What this script does
  1. Setup            clone official repo, install deps, load ViT-B/16 weights
  2. Data             load OpenDeepfake-Preview, stratified 70/15/15 split (seed 42)
  3. Baseline         frozen ViT features + logistic regression
  4. Fine-tuning      full fine-tuning (AdamW, lr 1e-5, batch 2), test evaluation
  5. Ablation         epochs 2-3 (analysis only; model chosen by validation loss)
  6. Duplicate audit  exact-duplicate (pixel hash) check on the evaluated split

Switch parts on/off in the CONFIG cell. Nothing is trained if a saved
checkpoint already exists (set FORCE_RETRAIN = True to override), so the
reported test results can be reproduced quickly from the checkpoint.
"""

